<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">First Anglo-Burmese War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1824–1826</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The First Anglo-Burmese War was fought between the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> and the Konbaung kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a>, which had conquered Arakan, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assam">Assam</a> and Manipur and pressed on British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a>. After costly campaigns and the capture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangon">Rangoon</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-yandabo">Treaty of Yandabo</a> in 1826 forced Burma to cede Arakan and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tanintharyi-region">Tenasserim</a>, pay a large indemnity and give up its claims to Assam and Manipur.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-anglo-burmese-war.jpg" alt="First Anglo-Burmese War" width="320" height="244" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: J. Moore · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_rangoon.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
